From: Fedora kitty package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] tests: skip unreliable utmp user count test

The test compares kitty's count of live USER_PROCESS records with the
unfiltered output of who.  Stale or concurrently removed utmp records can
make those values differ, so this is not a reliable build-time test.

---
 kitty_tests/utmp.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kitty_tests/utmp.py b/kitty_tests/utmp.py
index 7f62bd1..b31cc8c 100644
--- a/kitty_tests/utmp.py
+++ b/kitty_tests/utmp.py
@@ -9,2 +9,4 @@ class UTMPTest(BaseTest):
     def test_num_users(self):
+        self.skipTest('utmp records are unreliable in package build environments')
+
         # who is the control
-- 
